/* THE GOBLIN PRIEST's rite, in one place (updateGobPriest): its first rite can come `first` seconds after it spawns, so the goblins round it are blessed the moment it sees you; the censer
   is up for `tell` when a foe within `reach` px needs it, and then every foe within `smoke` px (the censer's cloud: a
   goblin that wandered a step off during the chant is still in it) is mended by `mend` of its health and BLESSED for
   `bless` s, taking `take` of every blow. A blow on the priest while the censer is up breaks it: dazed `daze` s, and `cd`
   again before the next. Its health is two of a knight's blows at the monastery: the first breaks the rite, the second
   finishes it */
for (const key of COMMON_BLOWS) if (DMG[key]) DMG[key] = Math.round(DMG[key]*COMBAT.commonDamage);
const PRIEST = { first: 0.3, tell: 1.5, cd: 7, reach: 110, smoke: 150, mend: 0.35, bless: 6, take: 0.5, daze: 1.4 };
/* THE GOBLIN MAGE's reach, in one place (updateGobMage). It sees you inside `sees` px, walks off to keep you `near`..`far` px
   away, throws a bolt that flies `reach` px at `boltV` px/s after a `boltTell` s yellow ! (every `boltCd` s), and writes a
   rune under your feet from inside `runeReach` px that goes off `runeTell` s after its red !! (every `runeCd` s); `gap` s
   between any two. Nothing it does reaches past 180 px: eleven tiles, a little over half the screen */
const MAGE = { sees: 220, near: 90, far: 150, speed: 40, reach: 180, boltV: 135, boltTell: 0.6, boltCd: 2.8, runeReach: 150, runeTell: 1.0, runeCd: 5.5, gap: 1.2 };
// THE METER PACES THE WRONG HALF OF THE FIGHT. A swing costs 12 and comes off the blade, so eight swings
// empty you and that is a fine rhythm - two full three-cut runs and then you breathe. But a DODGE cost 25,
// twice a swing, and the shield cost 16 a blow on top of 9 a second just to hold up: the meter taxed you
// hardest for the two things you do when you are losing. Defence is cheap now. Which of the two you reach
// for is the MARK's job to tell you - a yellow ! is the shield, a red !! is your feet - and that is a read,
// not an arithmetic problem about a bar.
const ST = { swing: 12, plunge: 28, dodge: 16, blockHit: 11, hold: 6, regen: 48, delay: 0.5 };

